{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1705","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Mark the Dust Sweeper"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mark is cleaning a row of $$$n$$$ rooms. The $$$i$$$-th room has a nonnegative dust level $$$a_i$$$. He has a magical cleaning machine that can do the following three-step operation. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select two indices $$$i \\lt j$$$ such that the dust levels $$$a_i$$$, $$$a_{i+1}$$$, $$$\\dots$$$, $$$a_{j-1}$$$ are all strictly greater than $$$0$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Set $$$a_i$$$ to $$$a_i-1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Set $$$a_j$$$ to $$$a_j+1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Mark's goal is to make $$$a_1 = a_2 = \\ldots = a_{n-1} = 0$$$ so that he can nicely sweep the $$$n$$$-th room. Determine the minimum number of operations needed to reach his goal."}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\leq t\\leq 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2\\leq n\\leq 2\\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of rooms."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1$$$, $$$a_2$$$, ..., $$$a_n$$$ ($$$0\\leq a_i\\leq 10^9$$$) — the dust level of each room."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ across all test cases does not exceed $$$2\\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a line containing a single integer — the minimum number of operations. It can be proven that there is a sequence of operations that meets the goal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n2 0 0\n5\n0 2 0 2 0\n6\n2 0 3 0 4 6\n4\n0 0 0 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n5\n11\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first case, one possible sequence of operations is as follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=1$$$ and $$$j=2$$$, yielding the array $$$[1,1,0]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=1$$$ and $$$j=3$$$, yielding the array $$$[0,1,1]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=2$$$ and $$$j=3$$$, yielding the array $$$[0,0,2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" At this point, $$$a_1=a_2=0$$$, completing the process."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second case, one possible sequence of operations is as follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=4$$$ and $$$j=5$$$, yielding the array $$$[0,2,0,1,1]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=2$$$ and $$$j=3$$$, yielding the array $$$[0,1,1,1,1]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=2$$$ and $$$j=5$$$, yielding the array $$$[0,0,1,1,2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=3$$$ and $$$j=5$$$, yielding the array $$$[0,0,0,1,3]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=4$$$ and $$$j=5$$$, yielding the array $$$[0,0,0,0,4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the last case, the array already satisfies the condition."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1705B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1705/problem/B"}